                <pb facs="0567" n="535" xml:id="pg535"/>

                <head>254. Memorandum From the Executive Secretary (Lay) to the National Security
                        Council<anchor n="1" xml:id="d254-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-09-16"><hi rendition="#italic">September 16,
                        1955</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>U.S. Policy in the Event of a Renewal of Aggression in Vietnam</item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>REFERENCES</head>
                    <item>A. NSC 5429/5, para. 5–d</item>
                    <item>B. NSC Action No. 1415</item>
                    <item>C. Memo for NSC Planning Board from Executive Secretary, same subject,
                        dated August 16, 1955<anchor n="2" xml:id="d254-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>The enclosed study, prepared by the Joint Chiefs of Staff in accordance with the
                    report adopted by the Planning Board on August 15 (Reference C) is transmitted
                    for the information of the National Security Council and the use of the NSC
                    Planning Board in its further consideration of the subject in connection with
                    carrying out NSC Action No. 1415–c.</p>
                <p>Also enclosed is a memorandum by the Deputy Secretary of Defense transmitting and
                    commenting on the JCS study.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">At the request of the Deputy Secretary of Defense, these
                        papers are being given a special limited distribution. It is requested that
                        special security precautions be observed in their handling and that access
                        to them be strictly limited on a need-to-know basis</hi>.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">James S. Lay, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[Here follows a table of contents.]</p>
                </postscript>



